10.9, "lean": 0.0, "environment": 8.3, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": 0.6}, "rating_margin": 8.25, "sigma_race": 6.2, "sigma_total": 6.88, "baseline_margin": 8.08, "analyst_adjustment": -0.08, "key_factors": ["Vasquez holds a large money edge: $2.4M cash on hand vs. $794K for Cunningham", "Raters lean Likely D (with Cook/Sabato at Lean D, Inside Elections at Tilt D) and markets price Vasquez at 92-95%", "Thin polling shows a closer race: +3 for Vasquez in September, in an even-PVI district", "D-friendly midterm environment adds to the incumbency advantage"], "rationale": "Vasquez combines incumbency, a roughly three-to-one fundraising advantage, and a favorable midterm environment, and prediction markets plus most raters place the race firmly in Likely Democratic territory. The lone recent poll shows a narrower margin, but a single September survey with limited sample carries little weight against the broader evidence.", "watch": "If additional polling confirms the tight September numbers, or heavy outside attack advertising moves the race, this could shift toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Gabe Vasquez (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Gabe Vasquez, the Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in a southern New Mexico district that is evenly split between the parties. He enters the fall with a large financial advantage, having raised $3.8 million to Greg Cunningham's $1.5 million, and leads in cash on hand $2.4 million to $794,000. Most race raters call the contest Likely Democratic, though Cook and Sabato rate it Lean Democratic and Inside Elections says Tilt Democratic.\n\nPrediction markets give Vasquez a 92 to 95 percent chance of winning. Polling is sparse: a September SurveyUSA survey put him ahead 46 to 43, and a Republican-sponsored spring poll showed a similarly narrow race. Attack advertising has flooded the district and the contest has drawn national attention, but incumbency, money, and a favorable midterm environment keep Vasquez the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8892, "margin": 7.53}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8688, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8708, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.87, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8306, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8384, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8302, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8733, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8614, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.875, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8706, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.896, "margin": 8.0}]}